                <pb facs="0857" n="843" sameAs="frus:frus1872p2v1/pg843"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Boutwell,
                        Secretary of the Treasury, to Mr. Rumley,
                        collector</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <dateline><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Treasury Department</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1869-10-05"><hi rendition="#italic">October</hi>
                        5, 1869</date>.</dateline>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">D. Rumley</hi>, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Collector of Customs, Wilmington, North
                    Carolina:</hi></p>
                <p>Your course in the case of the Hornet is approved. Who is retained as counsel?
                    You will hold the Hornet, under the eleventh section of the act of 1818, until
                    directed by the President to release her.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>GEO. S. BOUTWELL,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Secretary,
                        &amp;c.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
